<title>USA: Brady debt treads up, but all eyes on LDC issuance.</title>
<headline>Brady debt treads up, but all eyes on LDC issuance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emerging debt prices edged higher Thursday, but Brady bond dealers reported that most attention centered on the flood of new sovereign issuance over the past two days, traders said.</p>
<p>Emerging nations, among them Russia, Mexico, Argentina, Philippines and South Africa, took advantage of low rates and a global craving for yield by floating more than $5.0 of new debt over Wednesday and Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;That's a ton of paper,&quot; said the chief dealer at one major U.S. investment bank. &quot;We are a little bit saturated.&quot;</p>
</text>
